IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic) -- the four steps with a deadline, as regulative rules.
--
-- s 30(1) (take proceedings within 3 months of the personal representative's notice), s 70Q(1) (the personal
-- representative's right to elect notice within 30 days of the grant), s 70R(1) (the partner's property election within 3
-- months) and s 99(1) (a family provision application within 6 months of the grant). Each is a DEONTIC rule counted in plain
-- days from its start; the questions in ap-seat.l4 never take a DEONTIC or an EVENT: they take dates, and the rules are run
-- here by EVALTRACE.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Administration
-- and Probate Act 1958, Version No. 130 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Steps with a deadline`

DECLARE `Estate party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the personal representative`

DECLARE `Estate act` IS ONE OF
    `take all proceedings proper to enforce or establish the claim`
    `give the partner the right to elect notice`
    `make the partner's property election`
    `apply for a family provision order`

-- s 30(1): the personal representative "may serve upon any person making or possibly entitled to make such claim a notice
-- requiring such person to take within a period of three months from the date of receiving such notice all proceedings
-- proper to enforce or to establish such claim and to duly prosecute the same." (2), (3): after the three months the
-- personal representative may apply, and the Court, if not satisfied that proceedings have been taken and are being duly
-- prosecuted, may extend the period, bar the claim, or let the estate be distributed without regard to it.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
`s 30 -- the claimant must take proceedings within three months of the notice` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `take all proceedings proper to enforce or establish the claim`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "no proceedings within three months of receiving the notice: the personal representative may apply, and the Court may extend the time, bar the claim or let the estate be distributed without regard to it (s 30(2), (3))"

-- s 70Q(1): "within 30 days of the grant of administration of an intestate's estate, the personal representative must give
-- the partner of the intestate to whom this Division applies a written notice informing the partner of the partner's right
-- to make a partner's property election." (3): not required if the partner is the personal representative.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
`s 70Q -- the personal representative must give the right to elect notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the personal representative`
    MUST `give the partner the right to elect notice`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the personal representative` BECAUSE "no right to elect notice within 30 days of the grant of administration (s 70Q(1))"

-- s 70R(1): "A partner's property election must be made -- (a) if the partner is a personal representative of the intestate,
-- within 3 months of the grant of administration; or (b) if the partner is not a personal representative of the intestate,
-- within 3 months of the date of the right to elect notice ...; or (c) if the Court extends the time for making the election,
-- by the date to which the period for election is extended."
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
`s 70R -- the partner must make the election in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `make the partner's property election`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "no partner's property election in time: only if the Court extends the time, for sufficient cause and before the administration is completed (s 70R(1)(c), (2))"

-- s 99(1): "An application to the Court for a family provision order must be made within 6 months after the date of the grant
-- of probate of the will or of letters of administration". (2), (3): the Court may extend the period, on an application for
-- extension made before the final distribution of the estate.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
`s 99 -- the eligible person must apply within six months of the grant` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `apply for a family provision order`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "no family provision application within 6 months after the grant: only if the Court extends the period, on an application made before the final distribution of the estate (s 99(2), (3))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (in the shape of the Supreme Court Act 1986 and Accident Compensation Act
-- 1985 encodings). On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done,
-- FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in
-- time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the step` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
      `the party` IS AN `Estate party`
      `the act` IS AN `Estate act`
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`what became of` `the rule` `by` `the party` `with` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `at` `the time the act was done` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- The same, counted in plain days from a starting day to a last day, with the act done on a day or not yet done.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
      `the party` IS AN `Estate party`
      `the act` IS AN `Estate act`
      `the starting day` IS A DATE
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`the outcome of` `the rule` `by` `the party` `with` `the act` `counted from` `the starting day` `done` `the act has been done` `on` `the day the act was done` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` `the rule` `by` `the party` `with` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `at` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `the day the act was done`) `now` (`the days from` `the starting day` `to` `today`)
